  "claim_boundary": "This preregistered qualification evaluates the frozen v15.7 decision mechanism on 18 new globally held-out suite/task/init pairs. Actual MuJoCo arm mass, damping, or sliding friction is shifted while every counterfactual screening step uses the nominal shadow model; the actual model is restored before final execution. A matched nominal control and six one-factor mismatches are paired across identical lanes. The actual containment, liveness, force, and latency gates are unchanged. Exact same-model prediction identity is replaced before execution by a registered 0.01 rad mismatch-error envelope and explicit predicted/actual force-delta audit. A pass supports only empirical robustness to these bounded simulator model mismatches; it does not support attacked-task utility, hard-real-time, hardware, actuator-authority, arbitrary model error, or physical-safety claims.",
